# icons/items.rec: which sprite-sheet tile draws each items icon ID, one record each: items (item.<internal_name>), with .used / .magic / .unique variants where a mod has them.
# Every other file names icons by these IDs, never by number; an ID the game asks for that no record defines
# stops the game at start with its name.
# Fields:
#   internal_name     the icon ID, "kind.snake_case_name"
#   icon              the tile's number on the mod's sprite sheet (classic_roguelike.png), row by row from 0
#   name              a description for the mod author; not read
#   reference_image   the original graphic it stands in for; not read
#
# Heaven&Hell's item icons: sprite-sheet tiles by icon ID. Seeded from the numbers the item records
# carried before icons moved out of the content record.

